# Linux Setup Summary — Multi-Threaded Web Crawler

## What This Project Is
A C++ multi-threaded web crawler with graph analytics (PageRank, Tarjan SCC, Topological Sort), a Flask REST API, and an interactive dashboard. Built as a DAA course project.

---

## Step 1: Clone the Repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/ishaanparikh14/multithreaded-web-crawler.git
cd multithreaded-web-crawler
```

---

## Step 2: Install Dependencies
```bash
# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt update
sudo apt install cmake build-essential libcurl4-openssl-dev python3 python3-pip -y

# Fedora/CentOS
sudo dnf install cmake gcc-c++ libcurl-devel python3 python3-pip -y
```

---

## Step 3: Build the C++ Crawler
```bash
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make -j$(nproc)
cd ..
```

Binary will be at `./build/crawler`

---

## Step 4: Install Python Dependencies
```bash
pip3 install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Step 5: Run Everything

**Terminal 1 — API Server:**
```bash
python3 api_server.py
```
Runs on `http://localhost:5000`

**Terminal 2 — Dashboard:**
```bash
cd dashboard
python3 -m http.server 8080
```
Open browser: `http://localhost:8080`

---

## Step 6: Use the Dashboard
1. Enter a seed URL (e.g. `https://github.com`)
2. Choose strategy: `bfs`, `dfs`, or `priority`
3. Set max pages and threads
4. Click **Start Crawl**
5. Watch live progress
6. Results auto-load in Analytics and Benchmarks tabs

---

## Or Run Crawler Directly (No Dashboard)
```bash
./build/crawler https://github.com 50 4 bfs
```
CSVs are written to `output/` — then `python3 api_server.py` serves them.

